# Shell commands

Chat wrap breaks pasted commands mid-token. Keep every copyable line ≤80 chars.

## Pattern

```bash
d=~/Documents/facefusion
cd "$d"
source /opt/anaconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh
conda activate facefusion
PY=/opt/anaconda3/envs/facefusion/bin/python
```

Then invoke `$PY facefusion.py ...` — never bare `python`.

## Rules

- Never break a path, SHA, URL, or flag across lines
- Use `$HOME` or `~` to shorten paths
- Put commands in a fenced block alone — no prose on the same lines
- If continuation is needed, break only after a complete token with `\`

## Headless swap example

```bash
d=~/Documents/facefusion
cd "$d"
source /opt/anaconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh
conda activate facefusion
PY=/opt/anaconda3/envs/facefusion/bin/python
$PY facefusion.py headless-run \
  --config-path facefusion.ini \
  --target-path videos/example.mov \
  --source-paths faces/source.jpeg \
  --output-path output/example-out.mov \
  --processors face_swapper
```

Target and output extensions must match.
